# The rows of src/runtime/Live.h and src/runtime/Live.cpp, a call each (src/tools/bench/bench.py).

## Live.cpp/Builder::mount
1. a hosted -> "<here>/a\n"
2. b hosted, a still there -> "<here>/a\n<here>/b\n"
3. a gone, c hosted -> "<here>/b\n<here>/c\n"
4. c hosted again -> "<here>/b\n<here>/c\n"

## Live.cpp/Live::engine_changed
1. before: none
2. written: <here>/engine/a.cpp
3. asked again: none
4. both written at one time: <here>/engine/a.cpp

## Live.cpp/Live::poll
01. nothing written -> only none; failed []; built []; building false; errors ""
02. a file in v's .vulpen written -> only none; failed []; built []; building false; errors ""
03. a hidden file new in v's node folder -> started, failed; failed [v]; built [v]; building false; errors "Error: could not load cache\n"
04. a file of v written -> started, failed; failed [v]; built [v]; building false; errors "Error: could not load cache\n"
05. a file of w written -> started; failed [v]; built [w]; building true; errors "Error: could not load cache\n"
06. written again while it builds -> unsettled; failed [w]; built [w]; building false; errors "Error: could not load cache\n"
07. once the files settle -> started, failed; failed [w]; built [w]; building false; errors "Error: could not load cache\nError: could not load cache\n"
08. x watched, which the build has no target for -> started, succeeded; failed []; built [x]; building false; errors "Error: could not load cache\nError: could not load cache\n"
09. a file of x written -> started, succeeded; failed []; built [x]; building false; errors "Error: could not load cache\nError: could not load cache\n"
10. targets [vulpen_view_v, vulpen_view_w, vulpen_view_x]
11. v and x no longer watched: targets [vulpen_view_w]

## Live.cpp/Restart
1. not asked: ready false, asked false
2. a file of v written -> started, failed
3. quit restart -> vulpen builds; the run restarts once it is built, and goes on as it is if the build fails\n
4. again -> vulpen builds already; the run restarts once it is built\n
4b. the poll that starts its build -> ready false, building true; the next, the build waiting -> ready false
5. then ready false; its build ran true; asked false, building false; printed "<clock>            {!!!} quit restart: the build failed, so the ...not load cache\n" (185 characters, hash 7039cde23dd8f057)
6. without a live build, not asked -> ready false
7. quit restart again -> vulpen builds; the run restarts once it is built, and goes on as it is if the build fails\n
8. with no live build: its first poll ready false, building true; then ready false, asked false; printed "<clock>            {!!!} quit restart: the build failed, so the run goes on\n<clock>                  Error: could not load cache\n"

